<h1 id="earnings-results-disclaimer">Earnings &amp; Results Disclaimer</h1>
<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> <%= legalEffectiveDate %></p>
<p>127 teaches people how to start and grow a business and gives them the tools to do it. <strong>We don't promise that you'll make money.</strong></p>
<p><strong>No promise of income or results.</strong> Nothing from 127, whether on our website or app, in our AI tools, emails, social posts, ads, live streams, calls or events, is a promise or guarantee that you'll earn any amount of money, get customers, replace your income, or reach any other result.</p>
<p><strong>Your results depend on you, and on a lot no one controls.</strong> Your idea, skills, experience, time, money, market, competition, the economy and timing all matter. Starting a business is risky. Many new businesses never make a profit, and about 1 in 5 new US businesses close within their first year (U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics).</p>
<p><strong>Eli's story is his, not a forecast.</strong> When we share Eli's own results (for example, sales from his e-commerce brand, or leaving his corporate job to build full time), they're true examples from his life. They aren't typical, and they aren't what you should expect. He had his own experience, skills, network and timing.</p>
<p><strong>We don't publish what members earn.</strong> If we ever share a member's results, we'll have evidence for them and we'll say clearly what members generally achieve.</p>
<p><strong>Examples, calculators and AI responses are illustrations.</strong> Numbers in our playbooks, worksheets, calculators (like the Pricing Worksheet or the Launch Budget Calculator), examples and AI responses are hypothetical. They come from what you enter or from assumptions, and they aren't forecasts or promises.</p>
<p><strong>Education, not professional advice.</strong> 127 isn't financial, investment, legal, tax or accounting advice. Talk to a qualified professional before big decisions like quitting your job, borrowing money, investing, or signing a contract. Don't put in money you can't afford to lose.</p>
